' Reviewed implementation commit: pi-mono-java d03c08dbae870f19eee8d4fa79a707185f7a26b5 (Draft PR 181).
' Source evidence: frontend/README.md lines 26-28 and 40-58.
' Source evidence: frontend/.env.example lines 1-7.
' Source evidence: frontend/src/App.vue lines 177-290 and frontend/src/components/DevDiagnostics.vue lines 4-25.
' Source evidence: frontend/src/composables/useRuntimeApi.ts lines 18-20 and 480-495 (requestRaw).
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeSessionController.java.
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/test/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeSessionRoutesTest.java lines 102-120.
' Observed behavior: the current browser client calls Runtime V1 directly, sends only non-secret X-HW-ID, and has no JWT, APPKEY, or access-token editor, storage, or header injection path.
' Target-only design: the product browser calls a public bridge; an isolated internal development build may provide event-only debug headers.
' Design reason: diagnostic header transport is not production authentication; the public bridge owns identity, authorization, public resources, and safe event projection.

title CampusClaw product frontend boundary
left to right direction

actor "Campus user" as User
rectangle "Product frontend" as Frontend {
  component "Agent and chat workspace" as Workspace
  component "Product request adapter\ncredentialless" as RequestAdapter
  component "Product event projector" as Projector
  component "Developer diagnostics\n(internal build only)" as Diagnostics
}

rectangle "mate-service" as Mate {
  component "Public chat API" as PublicApi
  component "Chat to session mapping" as Mapping
  component "Auth, policy, and event projection" as Policy
}

rectangle "CampusClaw Runtime V1" as Runtime {
  component "Session controllers" as Sessions
  component "Request-scoped SSE" as Stream
}

User --> Workspace : chat tasks
Workspace --> RequestAdapter : product actions
RequestAdapter --> PublicApi : target public HTTP and SSE
PublicApi --> Policy
Policy --> Mapping
Mapping --> Sessions : internal HTTP
Stream --> Policy : internal SSE events
Policy --> Projector : public safe events
RequestAdapter ..> Sessions : current internal-only direct HTTP
Stream ..> Projector : current internal-only direct SSE
Diagnostics --> RequestAdapter : product-safe diagnostics only

note bottom of Frontend
Product constraints:
- No product Service URL or credential editor
- No JWT, APPKEY, or access-token product storage
- No raw session_id, ETag, JSON, or SSE frames
- Agent, chat, and attachment metadata use public resources
end note

note bottom of Mate
Security hardening:
- Establish identity outside Chat credential forms
- Exact browser session mechanism remains pending
- Authorize each action
- Project internal errors and events
- Do not byte-forward internal SSE
end note

note bottom of Runtime
Observed internal contract:
- 11 Session Runtime operations
- One active execution per Session
- No Runtime-local integration credential validation
- Persistent Entry history plus transient progress events
end note
@enduml

@startuml frontend_debug_header_flow
' Source baseline: pi-mono-java 320d790726a70aada6100052952d5494d2a378ac.
' Reviewed implementation commit: pi-mono-java d03c08dbae870f19eee8d4fa79a707185f7a26b5 (Draft PR 181).
' Source evidence: frontend/src/components/DevDiagnostics.vue lines 1-26.
' Source evidence: frontend/src/composables/useRuntimeApi.ts lines 139-155 and 480-497 (sendMessage and requestRaw).
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeEventController.java lines 58-73 (submit).
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeRequestContext.java lines 45-50 (mateCredentials).
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/common/client/HttpMateToolClient.java lines 93-190 and 298-373.
' Observed behavior: the current frontend has no credential controls and requestRaw always sends only non-secret X-HW-ID context.
' Observed behavior: the source baseline captures three headers on event submission and also sends them on discovery requests.
' Reviewed implementation: access-token is captured, discovery is credentialless, and only Mate tool execute receives the execution snapshot.
' Target-only frontend design: the debug drawer and event-only browser header snapshot are not implemented at the reviewed commit.
' Security hardening: fixed header names, memory-only values, event-only request scope, redacted diagnostics, and no automatic POST replay.
' Design reason: developers need fast credential propagation tests without turning the product browser into a credential manager.

title Internal debug header flow
left to right direction

actor "Developer" as Developer

rectangle "Internal development frontend" as DevFrontend {
  component "Debug header drawer\nfixed names and modes" as Drawer
  component "In-memory header state\nclear on reload" as HeaderState
  component "Event-only request adapter\nimmutable snapshot" as EventAdapter
}

rectangle "CampusClaw Runtime V1" as Runtime {
  component "POST sessions/{sessionId}/events\nRuntimeEventController.submit" as Submit
  component "RuntimeRequestContext\nexecution credential snapshot" as Snapshot
  component "Agent execution context" as Execution
}

rectangle "mate-service" as Mate {
  component "Agent, Skill, and tool metadata\ndiscovery without credentials" as Discovery
  component "POST runtime/tools/{toolId}/execute\ncredential headers attached" as Execute
}

Developer --> Drawer : enter temporary values
Drawer --> HeaderState : apply or clear
HeaderState --> EventAdapter : snapshot on message submit
EventAdapter --> Submit : initial event POST only
Submit --> Snapshot : capture request headers
Snapshot --> Execution : immutable for this execution
Execution --> Discovery : discover tools
Execution --> Execute : invoke a selected tool

note bottom of Drawer
Allowed header names:
- X-HW-ID
- Authorization
- X-HW-APPKEY
- access-token

Secret inputs are masked by default.
Browser DevTools can still inspect wire headers.
end note

note bottom of EventAdapter
Never attach the debug snapshot to:
- Session create, read, or delete
- History, model, or thinking
- Steer, FollowUp, or Abort

Do not replay the event POST after disconnect.
end note

note bottom of Runtime
Runtime transport behavior:
- Capture values without authenticating them
- Do not persist values in Session or events
- Later edits affect only the next execution
- Dual credentials are an internal diagnostic case
end note

note bottom of Mate
Reviewed feature implementation:
- Discovery receives no credential snapshot
- Tool execute receives configured values
- Missing required values fail before outbound call
- Logs and errors show presence only
end note
@enduml

@startuml assistant_rich_text_rendering
